# Chosen to match the C++ already in cpp/, not to impose a new style: the
# sources are 2-space indented, put the & and * with the type name, and the
# longest existing line is 99 columns.
#
# The commit that added this file also carries a one-off reformat of cpp/.
# It is not a no-op, and the honest reason is that "already conformant"
# depends on which clang-format runs: a local 21.1.7 reported zero diffs
# against these same settings, while the pinned hook rewrote include order
# and the indentation of directives inside #if blocks. The pinned version is
# the one that decides, so the tree is normalised to it here and later diffs
# are real changes rather than version drift.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 100
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Right
